.TH DCOMP 1 "August 2026" "DComp 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
dcomp \- apply declarative component systems to Docker
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B dcomp
.RI [ --state-root\ DIR ]
.I command
.RI [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B dcomp
manages the containers, networks, volumes, and recovery records belonging to a
declarative component system. It is a command-line tool, not a daemon.
.PP
Cyclo invokes DComp with an installation-specific state root. Run it as a
non-root user with access to the local Docker socket.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B version --json
Print the stable machine-readable version and API document.
.TP
.B apply
Apply a component-system declaration.
.TP
.B status
Print a component-system status document.
.TP
.B down
Stop and remove a component system.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR dcomp-healthcheck (1)
